WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.617
Week seven.

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:03.681
Strategy in a creative agency,

00:00:03.731 --> 00:00:04.778
with Tim Collier,

00:00:04.828 --> 00:00:07.443
National Head of Strategy at Cummins and Partners.

00:00:07.493 --> 00:00:11.194
His advice: be curious, and be opinionated.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:12.994
A planner informs what the work says, and why it will work.

00:00:13.044 --> 00:00:17.015
The client brings a business problem,

00:00:17.065 --> 00:00:18.631
creatives bring the idea,

00:00:18.681 --> 00:00:20.187
and strategy sits between,

00:00:20.237 --> 00:00:22.210
speaking for the audience.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.565
Planning was born in 1974, in Stephen King's Planning Guide at JWT London.

00:00:26.615 --> 00:00:30.350
A method must stimulate imagination,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:31.718
not just control it:

00:00:31.768 --> 00:00:32.568
realistic,

00:00:32.593 --> 00:00:33.393
pragmatic,

00:00:33.395 --> 00:00:35.658
fundamental and structured.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.841
Planning has since split into three jobs.

00:00:38.891 --> 00:00:41.293
Brand planners own what's said and why.

00:00:41.343 --> 00:00:44.690
Comms planners own where, when and in what order.

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:47.349
Media planners own who sees it.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.365
Brand planning is the underlying message.

00:00:50.415 --> 00:00:51.556
Not just do it,

00:00:51.606 --> 00:00:54.287
but I can be an athlete if I just try.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.967
The job is reading, research, writing, consulting and leading.

00:00:57.017 --> 00:01:03.750
Writing is the real skill: one page that inspires the creatives.

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:08.143
Tim wanted to design for General Pants, but did marketing work experience there.

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:08.993
The people he met that week got him a decade of jobs.

00:01:08.983 --> 00:01:14.249
People who get jobs know people.

00:01:14.933 --> 00:01:17.619
On social, stop thinking like a user.

00:01:17.669 --> 00:01:20.166
Media is cheap, so use scale.

00:01:20.216 --> 00:01:22.961
Don't blend in with the algorithm; stand out.

00:01:23.011 --> 00:01:25.939
Don't scam it either, it's a black box.

00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:31.807
A strategist works in four steps: discover, synthesis, plan and instruct.

00:01:31.857 --> 00:01:32.657
The client hands you a five page brief with everything under the sun.

00:01:32.612 --> 00:01:37.927
Your first job is subtraction.

00:01:38.633 --> 00:01:44.857
To discover, use the five Cs: company, culture, category, connections and consumer.

00:01:44.907 --> 00:01:47.095
Mostly desk research.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.130
Bill Bernbach said nothing is so powerful as an insight into human nature.

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:55.050
So watch people, and enjoy how strange they are.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.398
Frameworks add discipline, not the insight.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:01:59.970
The basic brief is get, who, to, by.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:00.820
Get inspiring athletes,

00:02:00.515 --> 00:02:01.315
who just did this,

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:01.810
to repurchase,

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:07.826
by reminding them of something.

00:02:08.533 --> 00:02:11.396
The single minded proposition is the hardest part.

00:02:11.446 --> 00:02:12.658
It's an invitation, not a claim.

00:02:12.708 --> 00:02:15.523
Not our chocolate is the richest,

00:02:15.573 --> 00:02:17.551
but what the richest chocolate tastes like,

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.251
and this is ours.

00:02:19.967 --> 00:02:21.049
To write a brief:

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:22.051
gather everything,

00:02:22.101 --> 00:02:23.349
write the task plainly,

00:02:23.399 --> 00:02:24.563
get to a point of view,

00:02:24.613 --> 00:02:26.226
then rewrite and recap.

00:02:26.276 --> 00:02:29.461
Without a point of view, it's just a summary.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.450
Then the planning cycle:

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:32.300
where are we,

00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:33.242
why are we there,

00:02:33.292 --> 00:02:34.221
where could we be,

00:02:34.271 --> 00:02:35.270
how could we get there,

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:36.485
and are we getting there?

00:02:36.535 --> 00:02:38.389
Then round again.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:43.118
The Effie is the strategist's award, the only one that matters to Tim.

00:02:43.168 --> 00:02:46.267
It takes a four thousand word essay proving the campaign worked,

00:02:46.317 --> 00:02:48.618
because strategy leads to profit.

00:02:49.333 --> 00:02:51.099
And we owe our clients.

00:02:51.149 --> 00:02:54.778
If an agency does a bad job, it probably won't get fired.

00:02:54.828 --> 00:02:57.147
The people in the factory will.

00:02:57.833 --> 00:03:00.472
So learn, process, apply.

00:03:00.522 --> 00:03:05.366
Nobody reads advertising; people read what interests them, and sometimes it's an ad.

00:03:05.416 --> 00:03:07.370
Be curious and opinionated.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.223
That's week seven.
